                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "57846017",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198002678333",
                            "num_reviews": 6,
                            "playtime_forever": 5021,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 4111,
                            "last_played": 1574878057
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Really fun game with a lot of character customization, multiple classes with unique abilities/upgrade paths, and lots of different possible playstyles. I've played mostly on some of the lower difficulty levels, which probably allowed me to progress further than I would have otherwise thanks to permadeath. On lower difficulty, you can freely explore and blow up aliens and robots at your leisure, while learning the game mechanics and picking up tips that will save your bacon when you ramp up the difficulty (Oh, you used your last action point to move around a corner and ran into a Ripsaw? RIP. Hopefully your replacement marine will have learned from its predecessor).\n\nParticularly enjoyed some of the features that I haven't really seen before in other games, notably, a unique class effect that grants different benefits upon breaching entryways, which gives a lot of additional complexity and strategic possibilities, and the randomized (and often hilarious) effect at the beginning of each turn which can give a much-needed boost, or wreck the delicate planning you had in place. \n\nThe procedural generation yields lots of replayability (and some very odd/unique map layouts), and I'm looking forward to what the polished final project looks like, give it a shot, and leave some feedback for the dev!",
                        "timestamp_created": 1574724324,
